Subject: vlandev: reject an explicitly empty VLAN identifier

An unset VID keeps the existing default in vlandev_config_init().
An explicitly empty string is not VLAN 0: strtoul() consumes no digits
but returns zero and leaves the end pointer at the terminating NUL.
Reject it before parsing without changing numeric VID 0 or alias lookup.

--- a/vlandev.c
+++ b/vlandev.c
@@ -257,6 +257,9 @@ vlandev_get_vid(struct device *dev, const char *id_str)
 	unsigned int *alias_id;
 	char *err;
 
+	if (!*id_str)
+		return -1;
+
 	id = strtoul(id_str, &err, 10);
 	if (err && *err) {
 		if (!dev)
